# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public-testnet E2E dev wallet — TEMPLATE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env.e2e.local` (gitignored) and fill in a DEDICATED,
# TESTNET-ONLY BIP-39 mnemonic. NEVER use a seed that has ever held mainnet
# funds — the derived keys submit real transactions on Base Sepolia, Solana
# devnet, and Mina devnet.
#
#   cp .env.e2e.example .env.e2e.local
#   node scripts/e2e-wallet.mjs generate     # prints a fresh mnemonic
#   # paste it below, then:
#   node scripts/e2e-wallet.mjs addresses    # prints the addresses to fund
#
# Put the SAME mnemonic into the org GitHub Actions secret `E2E_DEV_MNEMONIC`
# so CI (nightly public-testnet gate) derives the identical keys. See
# docs/e2e-testnets.md for the full bootstrap runbook.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The funded testnet dev wallet (12 or 24 BIP-39 words). One seed → all chains.
E2E_DEV_MNEMONIC=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional RPC / endpoint overrides. Defaults live in e2e/testnets.json.
# Override here when you need a private/API-keyed endpoint (e.g. Alchemy for
# Base Sepolia) — API-keyed URLs are secrets, keep them out of git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BASE_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=""
# SOLANA_DEVNET_RPC_URL=""
# MINA_DEVNET_GRAPHQL_URL=""
